---
// Device-flow sign-in and submission for agents. Values come from the build so the commands are ready to run.
import { Code, Steps } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';

const api = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_SUBMIT_API || 'https://<submit-endpoint>';
const clientId = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_ID || '<client-id>';
const ask = `curl -s -X POST https://github.com/login/device/code \\
  -H "Accept: application/json" -d client_id=${clientId}`;
const exchange = `curl -s -X POST https://github.com/login/oauth/access_token \\
  -H "Accept: application/json" -d client_id=${clientId} \\
  -d device_code=DEVICE_CODE \\
  -d grant_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:device_code`;
const submit = `curl -s -X POST ${api}/submit \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer ACCESS_TOKEN" \\
  -d '{"release_url": "https://github.com/OWNER/REPO/releases/tag/TAG", "accept_terms": true}'`;
---

<Steps>

<ol>
	<li>
		<p>Request a device code from GitHub for the registry. The response contains a <code>device_code</code>, a <code>user_code</code>, and an <code>interval</code> in seconds.</p>
		<Code code={ask} lang="bash" />
	</li>
	<li>
		<p>Instruct the user to open <a href="https://github.com/login/device">github.com/login/device</a>, sign in, and enter the <code>user_code</code>. The registry requests read access only to public profile information and repository permissions.</p>
	</li>
	<li>
		<p>Exchange the device code for an access token. Repeat the request every <code>interval</code> seconds while the response status is <code>authorization_pending</code>, until GitHub returns an <code>access_token</code>.</p>
		<Code code={exchange} lang="bash" />
	</li>
	<li>
		<p>Submit the release URL. Set <code>"accept_terms": true</code> only after the user accepts the terms of use. If the user does not have write access to the paper repository, set <code>"authors_permission": true</code> only after the user confirms author approval.</p>
		<Code code={submit} lang="bash" />
	</li>
</ol>

</Steps>
